CON-10: let lateral withdrawals take pollutant mass at the node's concentration

A negative lateral inflow component (negative [INFLOWS] or API inflow,
aquifer-ward groundwater, negative DWF, RDII or interface flow) reduced the
node's net lateral flow, and quality routing mixed the mass of the positive
sources with that net flow. The withdrawn water carried no mass, so the node
concentration rose (to 200 mg/L for 10 cfs at 100 mg/L less 5 cfs), and under
KINWAVE a net withdrawal booked mass that never existed. Record the
withdrawals per node (TNode.latWithdrawal), mix the inflow mass with all the
water that carried it (qualrout_execute), and book the withdrawn mass at the
mixed concentration in removeOutflows() instead of only a net negative flow.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply CON-10_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/objects.h b/src/legacy/engine/objects.h
index 6b54d76..4d72c54 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/objects.h
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/objects.h
@@ -543,6 +543,7 @@ typedef struct
    double        oldFlowInflow;   // previous flow inflow
    double        oldNetInflow;    // previous net inflow
    double        qualInflow;      // inflow seen for quality routing (cfs)
+   double        latWithdrawal;   // negative lateral inflows (cfs, > 0)
    double        apiExtInflow;    // inflow from swmm_setValue function (cfs)
 }  TNode;
 
diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/qualrout.c b/src/legacy/engine/qualrout.c
index 1cf5ae1..136d292 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/qualrout.c
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/qualrout.c
@@ -117,6 +117,12 @@ void qualrout_execute(double tStep)
     {
         // --- get node inflow and average volume
         Node[j].qualInflow = Node[j].inflow;
+
+        // --- mix the inflow mass with all the lateral water that carried it
+        //     (withdrawals leave at the mixed concen. in removeOutflows;
+        //     dynwave leaves a negative net lateral flow out of Node.inflow)
+        Node[j].qualInflow += Node[j].latWithdrawal;
+        if ( RouteModel == DW ) Node[j].qualInflow += MIN(0.0, Node[j].newLatFlow);
         qIn = Node[j].qualInflow;
         vAvg = (Node[j].oldVolume + Node[j].newVolume) / 2.0;
 
